| `models.max_reply_bytes` | integer | `8388608` | a whole number, 1 or more | `models/limits.py` (`max_reply_bytes`); `models/openai_compatible.py`; `models/claude_code_headless.py` | Sets how many bytes one model reply may hold: `openai-compatible` reads the HTTP body in pieces and refuses it with a `RuntimeError` naming the endpoint and this key at one byte past the cap, never reading the rest, and `claude-code-headless` ends its CLI's session once either output stream passes it (`ChildOutputTooLarge`). Absent, the adapter writes `[using default] models.max_reply_bytes = 8388608` to stderr. | how long the reply may take: `models.timeout_seconds`; a request's size, which no setting bounds | always |
